:"sha256:5fbae7fb5f8b8941b8c1794b32c91b77fe93387f5ac479f18c77b407bac09556","file":"preprints/The-Bass-trace-conjecture-for-complex-group-rings-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":45,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"70525dafb2d64025743742712adf81aa1d9bc50b0792d26e49540e23ecc239f3","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Bass-trace-conjecture-for-complex-group-rings-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:5fbae7fb5f8b8941b8c1794b32c91b77fe93387f5ac479f18c77b407bac09556","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Bass-trace-conjecture-for-complex-group-rings-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L45"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:bass}\nLet $G$ be any discrete group. For every $x\\in K_0(\\C G)$ and every\ninfinite-order element $g\\in G$,\n\\[\n \\HS_G(x)([g]_G)=0.\n\\]\nEquivalently, if $\\con_{\\mathrm{fin}}(G)$ denotes the conjugacy classes of\nfinite-order elements, then\n\\[\n \\HS_G\\bigl(K_0(\\C G)\\bigr)\n \\subseteq\\bigoplus_{C\\in\\con_{\\mathrm{fin}}(G)}\\C C.\n\\]"}
